Third-party components this project depends on or references
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ComfyUI
  https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI
  This project is a ComfyUI custom node package. It depends on ComfyUI at
  runtime and builds on ComfyUI's official MiniMax H3 support, importing and
  calling comfy_extras/nodes_minimax_h3.py, comfy/ldm/minimax/*,
  comfy_extras/nodes_audio.py, comfy.nested_tensor, comfy.model_patcher,
  comfy.model_management, comfy.sd and folder_paths from the installed ComfyUI.
  ComfyUI source is NOT vendored, copied or redistributed here: nothing under
  this repository contains ComfyUI code, and the package is useless without a
  separate ComfyUI installation that the user provides.
  Two exceptions are stated plainly rather than hidden:
    - raven_streaming/layout.py reimplements the frame-grid and canvas
      arithmetic that exists upstream as private module-level helpers
      (align_frame_count, video_latent_t, temporal_shape, adapt_canvas), because
      importing private helpers would be worse; the reimplementation is
      cross-checked against upstream in tests.
    - raven_streaming/causal_model.py subclasses upstream's MiniMaxH3Model to
      add chunk-causal attention; it derives from the installed class rather
      than copying it.
  ComfyUI is distributed under its own license (GPL-3.0 as of the audited
  baseline); consult the upstream repository for the authoritative terms.

MiniMax H3
  MiniMax H3 is a joint video + audio generation model developed by MiniMax.
  Weights used by this project are obtained by the user, e.g. from the
  Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3 repackaged repository on Hugging Face.
  This project does not distribute MiniMax H3 weights and does not download them
  automatically. The weights are subject to the license and usage terms
  published by their authors, which are separate from and independent of this
  repository's MIT license. Users must obtain the weights themselves and comply
  with those terms.

RAVEN
  This project requires a RAVEN streaming LoRA for MiniMax H3, obtained by the
  user, e.g. from the mvp-lab/MiniMax-H3-RAVEN-Streaming-LoRA repository on
  Hugging Face. The LoRA weights are not distributed here and are subject to
  their own license and usage terms, separate from and independent of this
  repository's MIT license.
  The sampling procedure implemented in raven_streaming/consistency.py,
  raven_streaming/cache.py and raven_streaming/causal_model.py is an
  independent implementation written against the RAVEN method as published by
  its authors (chunk-major fresh-noise consistency rollout, attention-sink plus
  sliding-window KV retention, per-stream trailing timestep grids). It is a
  reimplementation for ComfyUI, not a copy of a RAVEN codebase, and it carries
  no endorsement from the RAVEN authors. Anyone with rights questions about the
  method or the adapter should consult the RAVEN publication and the LoRA
  repository's own license.

PEFT / LoRA format
  The adapter file is a plain safetensors PEFT dump. This project parses that
  format and reproduces the arithmetic of peft.tuners.lora.layer.Linear.forward
  in raven_streaming/runtime_linear.py. The PEFT library itself is not a
  dependency and no PEFT code is included.

PyAV (av)
  https://github.com/PyAV-Org/PyAV
  A declared runtime dependency, used for fragmented MP4 (fMP4) muxing of the
  streamed preview segments. Not vendored. Distributed under its own license.
  PyAV in turn wraps FFmpeg, whose encoders (libx264, AAC, h264_nvenc, ...) are
  provided by whatever PyAV build the user installs and carry their own licenses
  and, in some cases, patent considerations. This project selects among the
  encoders present; it ships none of them.

